  "body": "When building a set for built-in tag names, I've noticed that `<image />` is not included in neither of indices (neither https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#elements-3 nor https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/obsolete.html), and thus is not cross-linked from tokenizer, even though it has special processing.\n\nI understand that technically speaking, it's just a synonym for `img` and not an element on its own, but I believe that it would be nice to have it listed in either of those summary tables.\n\nI suggest we either add it near the `img` in regular tables so that we would have `image, img` group similarly to how we have group of `h1`, `h2`, ..., or include it into a table of obsolete elements with an explanation that it's just a synonym.\n\nThoughts?\n",
